# ClinicBridge project context

- **Project**: ClinicBridge Portal. **Domain**: healthcare / health-tourism (intake, clinic matching, leads, quotes, appointments).
- Personal-data (KVKK) and business-process actions need stricter reliability than casual chat.
- Do **not** change working product behavior without explicit scope.

## Canonical LLM provider policy

- **OpenAI** is the official production LLM provider (`lib/services/aiGateway.ts`, `openai` package).
- OpenAI covers: single-clinic assistants, Clinic Portals, Agency Portals, FeelinHealthy, white-label deployments, portal/widget surfaces, and internal AI workflows unless documented otherwise.
- **Anthropic/Claude** = architecture reference only — **not** runtime. Do not add Anthropic SDKs, Claude models, or Anthropic env vars.
- Provider migration only via an **explicit, separately scoped migration task**. Architecture work must not silently change the provider.

## Surface boundaries

- Agency-specific rules ≠ Clinic Portal / single-clinic defaults.
- Single-clinic rules ≠ Agency Portal defaults.
- Shared behavior must be marked **product-global**.

## Layers (keep distinct)

Conversational intelligence (OpenAI) · deterministic business logic · domain services · persistence · side effects · UI · monitoring/evals.

Prefer extending `lib/agency/`, `lib/services/`, `app/api/public/` over parallel stacks.
